 @Lock2002ful  They're also talking about the new DLSS upscaling transformer model. And that's where they finally came clean about DLSS disadvantages - they were comparing current model to transformer model, not Frame Gen, and I was referring to that part of the video. It starts at 4:30. 

DLSS Quality 4k is definitely not as sharp and detailed as native. Let me guess, you sit too far away from the screen to notice? I have a 55 inch LG C2 and for that size recommended viewing distance is about 1,5-1,7m. At that distance I can easily tell the difference between 4k DLSS Quality (1440p) and native 4k. Obviously native 4k destroys DLSS Quality. What's more, in recent DF Directs John was alluding that he's not also 100% on DLSS hype train and that he can tell the difference. That's not really shocking, since it's very easy to tell the difference. It's just good to know that not all DF staff is on Nvidia's coolaid.

The further away you sit, the less you get from the extra pixel jump from 1080p to 4k. IIRC there was a study by THX (or maybe it was Dolby?), and it turned out that if you sit further than 5m from the screen you lose all the benefits of 4k screen and you could just stick to 1080p because you won't see any difference. So yeah...

